fact WorkItem(id: "WI-258", description: some(value: "Rc<TypingEnv> with copy-on-write mutation for the iterative typer. WI-255 made type_check_node iterative; each Visit op now stores TypingEnv by value, so pushing a child Visit clones the HashMap. For an Apply with N args, that's N HashMap clones where the recursive version had zero (it passed &TypingEnv). Wrap TypingEnv in Rc<TypingEnv>; the only mutating call sites (Let body, Lambda body, Match branch body — all of which already build a fresh env via extend_env_from_pattern) clone-on-write. Saves N-1 HashMap clones per multi-arg call site on deep specs. Acceptance: typing_pass_spec_parses_and_loads still passes on default 2 MiB stack; full workspace green; optional bench shows typer wall-clock reduction on typing_pass_spec."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-16T17:10:49Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-258", author: "user", content: "Delivered as part of combined commit e5611b6 (WI-258 + WI-259). TypeWorkOp::Visit and the env-carrying Build frames (Apply, Constructor, MatchAfterScrutinee.outer_env, MatchFinal.outer_env + branch_envs, LambdaBody.outer_env) now hold Rc<TypingEnv>. Child Visit pushes use Rc::clone (refcount bump) instead of HashMap clone. New unwrap_env(Rc<TypingEnv>) helper materializes via Rc::try_unwrap or fallback inner-clone for TypeResult-construction sites. LetAfterValue now decomposes value_r directly (r.env moves into ext_env, r.effects into the new LetFinal { value_effects } frame) — eliminates the value_r.env.clone() that paid for the body's ext_env base. Public type_check_node(&TypingEnv, ...) signature unchanged; TypeResult.env stays value-typed TypingEnv (public API stable). Full anthill-core suite green. Perf measurement deferred.", at: "2026-05-16T17:11:02Z")
